 "answer": "Ollama uses a **32k context** by default on a GPU with 32 GiB of VRAM, because that falls in the 24–48 GiB tier. The docs say: \"24-48 GiB VRAM: 32k context\" [ollama/docs/context-length.md].\n\nThe FAQ gives a different default: \"By default, Ollama uses a context window size of 4096 tokens.\" [ollama/docs/faq.md]. The documents don't say which is current, so I can't resolve the conflict. The VRAM-tiered figure is the more specific one for your case, but you can confirm the context actually in use with `ollama ps`, which shows a CONTEXT column [ollama/docs/context-length.md].",
